<title>USA: Kitty Hawk provides two new cargo planes.</title>
<headline>Kitty Hawk provides two new cargo planes.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kitty Hawk Inc said on Tuesday it is providing two additional Boeing 727-200 cargo aircraft to Burlington Air Express under a two-year contract plus options.</p>
<p>Kitty Hawk operates flights for Burlington Air throughout the western, southwestern, and midwestern United States, and also Mexico.</p>
<p>Kitty Hawk said said the two new aircraft are expected to account for about $13 million in annualized revenues.</p>
</text>
